*  118 - *outer dereferenced before outer is assigned.
*  Originally this test was meant to cover ARBNO+*var+FENCE seal
*  semantics, but the assignment of `outer` appears AFTER the match
*  statement.  In SNOBOL4, statements execute in source order, so
*  *outer dereferences an unassigned variable at match time and the
*  match fails immediately — the FENCE machinery is never exercised.
*  Both csnobol4 and SPITBOL agree on the outcome (NULL pattern fails).
*  Test 149 covers what 118 was originally meant to test.
        cmd = FENCE('a' | 'ab')
        s = 'aab'
        s POS(0) *outer RPOS(0)                               :S(BAD)F(GOOD)
        outer = ARBNO(*cmd)
BAD     OUTPUT = 'should fail (alt was tried)'                :(END)
GOOD    OUTPUT = 'arbno-star-cmd FENCE sealed'
END
